  "worked_solution": "First, we find ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ and $\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{3}{t}-{t}^{3})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e86,\\,\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}-3{t}^{2}\u27e9 \\\\ \u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}-3{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{4+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}-2+{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}+2+{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+{t}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}3(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3(-\\frac{1}{t}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}){|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{3}{t}+{t}^{3}){|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(-1+27)-(-3+1) \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$",
